  "text": "Science & Exploration Cluster Measuring Earth's magnetic environment The mission Cluster was a constellation of four spacecraft investigating the interaction between the Sun and Earth’s magnetosphere in unparalleled detail. The magnetosphere is our shield against the charged gas that carries particles and magnetic fields outwards from the Sun. Launch: 16 July and 9 August 2000 Mission end: 8 September 2024 Observed: solar wind, magnetosphere Orbit: elliptical around Earth’s poles, a few hundred to 125 000 km altitude Spacecraft names: Rumba, Salsa, Samba and Tango 11 instruments 4 spacecraft 2 decades of operation Latest All Stories Videos Images Story Space Safety Moving satellites to meet a plane for rare reentry data 02/02/2026 6273 views 31 likes Read Video 00:46:03 Science & Exploration Seas of the Sun: The story of Cluster 31/10/2025 3547 views 39 likes Play Image Science & Exploration Seas of the Sun: The story of Cluster poster 21/10/2025 1185 views 21 likes View Story Science & Exploration Goodnight, Cluster: brilliant end to trailblazing mission 09/09/2024 12301 views 54 likes Read Video 00:06:50 Science & Exploration Cluster reentry explained: world's first targeted reentry 08/09/2024 16361 views 65 likes Play Video 00:01:02 Science & Exploration Cluster’s Salsa satellite primed to reenter and break up 30/08/2024 5143 views 49 likes Play Story Space Safety Watching Salsa’s reentry live from the sky 26/08/2024 7722 views 31 likes Read Story Science & Exploration Cluster mission set to end with reentry over South Pacific 22/08/2024 7189 views 46 likes Read Image Science & Exploration Cluster explains spiral dance seen over Norway 25/03/2024 3103 views 40 likes View Story Enabling & Support Salsa’s last dance targets reentry over South Pacific 26/01/2024 5116 views 36 likes Read Image Science & Exploration The foreshock in Earth’s magnetic environment 18/11/2019 8104 views 150 likes View Video 00:00:13 Science & Exploration Earth’s magnetic song d